Per-user OAuth connections are made in the ORGANIZATION DASHBOARD, in a
browser signed in to your org account: the dashboard starts the
attempt, the provider redirects back to the dashboard origin's
/connect/callback, and the connection is bound to the SAME signed-in
member. This node never handles the OAuth callback and never sees the
upstream token. `connect` prints that page's URL - on the dashboard
origin of the org this node is enrolled with (or --dashboard-url) - and
the per-user servers this node's accepted grant names. It makes no
network call; --open launches your browser on it.

Usage:
  observer mcp connect [--server <id>] [flags]

Flags:
      --config string          path to config.toml (default ~/.observer/config.toml)
      --dashboard-url string   org dashboard URL (default: the org server this node is enrolled with)
  -h, --help                   help for connect
      --json                   print JSON
      --open                   open the URL in the default browser
      --server string          registry MCP server id to connect
